      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should be described in the javadoc for this function.\n\nAlso – what about having a reused temp object ? E.g.\n\n    final Entry temp \u003d new Entry(...);\n    stats.map(e -\u003e {\n        temp.uid \u003d UID_ALL\n        temp.set \u003d SET_ALL\n        temp.rxBytes \u003d e.rxBytes\n        ...\n        return temp;\n    });\n\nWill this work ? I think it will, right ? If so, do you want to migrate the implementation of groupByIface and groupByUid to this ?\n\nMoreover – now that you\u0027re using combineValue, IIUC this actually never takes a ref to the passed entry. So... it would actually work to mutate the returned entry ? If it would, then you should just remove this restriction and allow it, because it\u0027s most memory efficient and really intuitive.",
